  "description": "`completed_at` is present iff `todo_state = 'DONE'` on every path that writes the state (`write_todo_timestamp_transitions_in_tx`, #5074): stamped on an edge into DONE, cleared on an edge out of it and when a DONE block stops being a task, and never written for an open state. The stamp carries today's date, which the snapshot and the op digest drop, so the ops run through the command leg (`via: \"command\"`; the payload replay writes only the `todo_state` column) and a `query_by_property` step reads WHICH blocks hold one. Seed: S1 (Tasks) > S2 (DONE), S3 (DONE then TODO), S4 (DONE then cleared), S5 (DOING), S6 (DONE by `set_todo_state_batch`), S7 (DONE by `set_property_batch`). Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
